## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a streaming NLP system that handles multiple languages, domain adaptation, drift monitoring, latency budgets, and privacy considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual NER with adapters
- Drift monitoring and active learning
- Domain gazetteers and retrieval augmentation
- Privacy: data minimization and differential privacy
- Evaluation: streaming metrics, latency budgets, OOD checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference sketch with adapters
async function predict(text, model) {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const enc = model.encode(tokens);
  const logits = await model.predict(enc);
  return decodeEntities(logits, tokens);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify and react to drift in production?
- How would you structure the entity schema with provenance and versioning?
- How would you audit and mitigate bias across languages?

## Why This Is Questioned

This question evaluates end-to-end system design with competing constraints: real-time performance, multilingual support, strict privacy requirements, and operational scalability across tenants.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- On-device privacy preservation
- Multilingual ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition)
- Differential privacy (DP) embeddings
- Edge inference
- Model drift detection
- Human-in-the-loop annotation

## Code Example

```javascript
async function processAudioChunk(chunk, tenantId) {
  const text = await asrOnDevice(chunk, tenantId);
  const redacted = await redactPII(text, tenantId);
  const signal = await applyDifferentialPrivacy(redacted, tenantId);

  if (signal.riskScore > config.threshold) {
    await routeToTriageQueue(signal, tenantId);
  }
  return signal;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design modular, scalable NLP systems that evolve without full retraining, while meeting strict latency and privacy constraints across multiple languages.

## Key Concepts
- Adapter-based fine-tuning
- Multilingual encoders
- Real-time latency requirements
- Privacy-preserving logging
- Canary rollout and drift detection

## Code Example
